      ],
      "explanation": "To add the fractions, give them the common denominator \\(6x\\), which is nonzero because \\(x\\ne0\\). Then\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac1x+\\frac1{2x}+\\frac1{3x}\n&=\\frac6{6x}+\\frac3{6x}+\\frac2{6x}\\\\\n&=\\frac{6+3+2}{6x}\\\\\n&=\\frac{11}{6x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac{11}{6x}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
      "id": "common-denominator",
